<title>USA: King County, Wash., $150 mln repriced, yields cut.</title>
<headline>King County, Wash., $150 mln repriced, yields cut.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Smith Barney Inc. said Tuesday it repriced King County, Wash., $150 million bond deal, cutting yields in several maturities.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:</p>
<p>KING COUNTY, WASHINGTON</p>
<p>RE: $150,000,000*</p>
<p>LIMITED TAX GENERAL OBLIGATION BONDS</p>
<p>1997 SERIES D</p>
<p>(BASEBALL STADIUM)</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD.</p>
<p>PLEASE NOTE REPRICING OF THE ISSUE.</p>
<p>					REMARKETING</p>
<p>MOODY'S: Aa1		   S&amp;P: AA+</p>
<p>DATED: 04/17/1997	    FIRST COUPON: 12/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 12/01</p>
<p>ALL BONDS ARE PRICED AT PAR.</p>
<p> MATURITY		AMOUNT*    COUPON</p>
<p>12/01/1999		2,935M    4.60  %</p>
<p>12/01/2000		4,285M    4.80  %</p>
<p>12/01/2001		5,435M    4.95  %</p>
<p>12/01/2002		6,705M    5.10  %</p>
<p>12/01/2003		8,110M    5.20  %</p>
<p>12/01/2004		9,645M    5.25  %</p>
<p>12/01/2005	     11,325M    5.30  %</p>
<p>12/01/2006	     13,160M    5.40  %</p>
<p>12/01/2007	     15,165M    5.50  %</p>
<p>12/01/2008	     17,350M    5.55  %</p>
<p>12/01/2009	     19,730M    5.60  %</p>
<p>12/01/2010	     22,320M    5.70  %</p>
<p>12/01/2011	     13,835M    5.75  %</p>
<p>CALL FEATURES: 12/01/2007    102.00</p>
<p>		   DTP 12/01/2009</p>
<p>THE BONDS ARE SUBJECT TO EXTRAORDINARY MANDATORY REDEMPTION, IN WHOLE BUT NOT IN PART, ON OR BEFORE SEPTEMBER 11,1997 (OR SUCH LATER DATE DETERMINED IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE BOND ORDINANCE) AS FURTHER DESCRIBED IN THE P.O.S.IF THE BONDS ARE CALLED VIA THE EXTRAORDINARY REDEMPTION THEY WILL BE CALLED AT PAR.</p>
<p>* - APPROXIMATE SUBJECT TO CHANGE</p>
<p>The compliance addendum MSRB Rule G-11 will apply.</p>
<p>The award is expected ON APRIL 23, 1997.</p>
<p>Delivery is expected on May 7, 1997.</p>
<p>This issue is book entry through DTC.</p>
<p>Smith Barney Inc.</p>
<p>J.P. Morgan Securities Inc.</p>
<p>E.J. De La Rosa &amp; Co., Inc.</p>
<p>Siebert, Brandford, Shank &amp; Co.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
